# OSDP provider fixture corpus -- Phase 3 (capability negotiation and osdp_MFG).
#
# Vectors are spec-derived, not captured from hardware: frames are constructed
# per SIA OSDP v2.2.2 sec.5, their capability entries per sec.6.6, and their
# error checks computed by a bitwise CRC-16/AUG-CCITT reference written from the
# polynomial. That reference is checked against the Phase 1 corpus before it is
# trusted to produce this one.
#
# No record claims to be traffic from a named vendor's hardware. The two
# records mentioning HID use the one OUI this library relies on (00:06:8E) with
# a body of our own choosing; a wrong OUI silently routes a device to the wrong
# quirk set, so an unverified one is worse than none. See vendor.go.
#
# Format: '@name' opens a record, '!' is its description, ':key value' lines are
# the expectations the record asserts, and hex octets follow. Expectations are
# checked AFTER Provider.Reconcile, so a 'quirked' record states what the panel
# ends up believing, not what the device claimed.
#
# Records named bad-* carry a payload the codec must reject rather than guess at.

@cap-wall-reader
!osdp_PDCAP from a single-reader wall reader: the commonest device on any bus
:vendor generic
:readers 1
:leds 2
:buzzers 1
:displays 0
:inputs 4
:outputs 4
:secure true
:defaultkey false
:maxmessage 128
53 80 26 00 05 46 01 01 04 02 01 04 03 01 00 04 01 02 05 01 01 06 00 00 08 01
00 09 01 00 0A 80 00 0D 01 01 3A 50

@cap-two-reader-controller
!a two-reader door controller: per-reader counts stay per reader, never multiplied
:vendor hid
:readers 2
:leds 4
:buzzers 1
:displays 2
:inputs 8
:outputs 8
:secure true
:defaultkey false
:maxmessage 1024
53 82 26 00 06 46 01 02 08 02 01 08 03 01 00 04 02 04 05 01 01 06 02 02 08 01
00 09 01 00 0A 00 04 0D 01 02 C0 C7

@cap-secure-channel-absent
!osdp_CAP_COMMUNICATION_SECURITY reported at compliance 0: the device says no
:vendor generic
:readers 1
:leds 1
:buzzers 0
:displays 0
:inputs 2
:outputs 2
:secure false
:defaultkey false
:maxmessage 128
53 83 1D 00 07 46 01 01 02 02 01 02 04 01 01 08 01 00 09 00 00 0A 80 00 0D 01
01 CD 2F

@cap-default-key-in-use
!AES-128 capable but still holding SCBK-D; installable, not yet confidential
:vendor generic
:readers 1
:leds 1
:buzzers 1
:displays 0
:inputs 0
:outputs 0
:secure true
:defaultkey true
:maxmessage 256
53 84 1A 00 05 46 04 01 01 05 01 01 08 01 00 09 01 01 0A 00 01 0D 01 01 E2 FD

@cap-quirked-vendor
!a device claiming AES-128 and a 1024-octet buffer, corrected by its vendor quirks
:vendor quirked
:readers 1
:leds 2
:buzzers 1
:displays 0
:inputs 4
:outputs 4
:secure false
:defaultkey false
:maxmessage 128
53 85 20 00 06 46 01 01 04 02 01 04 04 01 02 05 01 01 08 01 00 09 01 00 0A 00
04 0D 01 01 21 89

@cap-unknown-function
!functions 0x11 and 0x7F, which this library does not name; they must survive
:vendor generic
:readers 1
:leds 1
:buzzers 0
:displays 0
:inputs 0
:outputs 0
:secure true
:defaultkey false
:maxmessage 128
53 86 1A 00 07 46 04 01 01 09 01 00 0A 80 00 0D 01 01 11 01 02 7F AA 55 D6 EB

@cap-checksum-framed
!a legacy device answering osdp_CAP inside a checksum frame rather than a CRC one
:vendor generic
:readers 1
:leds 0
:buzzers 0
:displays 0
:inputs 1
:outputs 1
:secure false
:defaultkey false
:maxmessage 0
53 87 13 00 01 46 01 01 01 02 01 01 08 00 00 0D 01 01 AE

@cap-empty
!an osdp_PDCAP carrying no entries; legal, unhelpful, and not a parse error
:vendor generic
:readers 0
:leds 0
:buzzers 0
:displays 0
:inputs 0
:outputs 0
:secure false
:defaultkey false
:maxmessage 0
53 88 08 00 06 46 D0 A8

@bad-cap-truncated
!an osdp_PDCAP cut mid-entry: 8 octets is not a whole number of triples
:vendor generic
:error short-payload
53 89 10 00 07 46 01 01 04 02 01 04 04 01 82 14

@mfg-hid-command
!osdp_MFG to an HID reader: OUI 00:06:8E and a vendor-defined body
:vendor hid
:oui 00068E
:recognised false
:body 01DEADBEEF
53 00 10 00 05 80 00 06 8E 01 DE AD BE EF D3 DB

@mfg-unknown-vendor
!a vendor with no provider registered; the body is carried, not discarded
:vendor generic
:oui ABCDEF
:recognised false
:body 7B226F6B223A317D
53 01 13 00 06 80 AB CD EF 7B 22 6F 6B 22 3A 31 7D 23 BA

@mfg-reply-passthrough
!osdp_MFGREP: the same body in the other direction, from the device
:vendor hid
:oui 00068E
:recognised false
:body 020001
53 80 0E 00 05 90 00 06 8E 02 00 01 21 EE

@mfg-empty-body
!an osdp_MFG that is nothing but an OUI; the shortest legal vendor message
:vendor hid
:oui 00068E
:recognised false
:body
53 02 0B 00 07 80 00 06 8E E9 51

@bad-mfg-short
!two octets where three are needed; the OUI itself is incomplete
:vendor generic
:error short-payload
53 03 0A 00 05 80 00 06 71 5B

